Package: weir
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mourty <Mourt2@proton.me>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@, pipewire, wireplumber, libxkbcommon0, libegl1
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Mourty/Weir
Description: Voicemeeter-style audio mixer for PipeWire
 Weir puts the sound on your computer on a mixing desk. Your microphone,
 your music, your browser and your game each get a strip with a fader.
 Your headphones, your speakers and a virtual microphone for Discord or OBS
 each get a bus, and a row of buttons beside every fader decides who hears
 what.
 .
 It installs three programs: weir-daemon, the background service that does
 the mixing; weir, the mixer window; and weirctl, a command line for
 scripts and stream decks.
